# Ship trade route with a Europe stop across six turns. Base: turns_spring_1600_events' output (France, Spring 1600, turn 108).
# Fixture: trade routes copied from map_trade_route_assign's output, route 1 rewritten to 2 stops: 0 = Europe (unload
# Tobacco + Furs, load Tools), 1 = Quebec (unload Tools); Caravel #121 (Tobacco 69 + Furs 39) on the high seas at (50,29),
# orders TRADE_ROUTE (2), route 1 stop 0 (profession byte 0x01 = stop<<4 | route), goto = its own tile, moves spent;
# every other French map unit fortified (orders 6), Caravel #148 (bound for Europe) parked in Quebec, France and England
# at peace (euro_relation 0x60 both ways, else English raids capture units).
# Turn 109 the route sails the Caravel for Europe; turn 111 it docks: the Europe screen opens with both holds sold
# (gold 429 -> 745) and 100 Tools bought (-> 145), it sails west with a dock colonist aboard; turn 113 it reappears at
# (50,29) and heads for Quebec; turn 114 it unloads the Tools in Quebec (stock 0 -> 100) and aims at the Europe stop again.
key space                  # end turn 108 (every unit has orders)
wait 300
key Return                 # Colonization Help: Time Scale
wait 60
key Return                 # Sons of Liberty in Quebec up to 60%
wait 60
key Return                 # price of Cigars rises to 11 (then the route ship sails for Europe)
wait 60
key space                  # end turn 109
wait 300
key Return                 # Iroquois gift (16 Ore) at Port au Prince
wait 60
key Return                 # King raises the tax by 1% (Kiss pinky ring, row 0)
wait 60
key Return                 # Sons of Liberty in Port au Prince up to 12%
wait 60
key Return                 # Sons of Liberty in Martinique up to 51%
wait 60
key Return                 # Sons of Liberty in Guadeloupe up to 70%
wait 60
key Return                 # new cargo of Horses at Montreal (storage full)
wait 60
key space                  # end turn 110
wait 300
key Return                 # Tupi gift (6 Tobacco) at Guadeloupe
wait 60
key Return                 # price of Cigars falls to 11
wait 60
key Return                 # price of Coats rises to 11; the Caravel docks, the route sells/buys, the Europe screen opens
wait 60
key e                      # leave Europe (the Caravel is already Bound for New France)
wait 30
key space                  # end turn 111 (no popups)
wait 300
key space                  # end turn 112
wait 300
key Return                 # Sons of Liberty in Port au Prince up to 21%
wait 60
key Return                 # Sons of Liberty in Martinique up to 61%
wait 60
key Return                 # price of Coats falls to 11 (the Caravel is back at (50,29))
wait 60
key Return                 # price of Trade Goods rises to 3; the Caravel sails toward Quebec
wait 60
key space                  # end turn 113
wait 300
key Return                 # Aztec food gift
wait 60
key Return                 # Tupi ask Montreal for food: row 0 declines
wait 60
key Return                 # Sons of Liberty in Guadeloupe up to 81%
wait 60
key Return                 # rebel sentiment 61%
wait 60
key Return                 # price of Cloth rises to 13
wait 60
key Return                 # price of Coats falls to 10; the Caravel enters Quebec and unloads the Tools, its passenger waits for orders
wait 60
